  "body": "## What changed\n\n- New post `assets/posts/g-edm.cps`, registry name \"G-EDM Wire EDM\". It serves `wire_edm` machines only. \"Generic ISO Wire EDM\" stays the default (`WIRE_POSTS[0]`).\n- The post writes Grbl-family words only: `G21` / `G20 G90 G17`, `G0` to the threading point, `G1`, `G2` / `G3` with incremental `I J`, and `M30`.\n- The post writes no `%` fence, no `O` word, no `F`, no `G40` / `G41` / `G42`, and no work offset word.\n- The post reads no `edm.codes`. The condition id is a comment. The header says that the operator sets the spark power at the controller.\n- The header has `(NOT VERIFIED ON A CONTROL - CHECK BEFORE CUTTING)`.\n- The post writes one vertical 2-axis wire section for each program.\n- These items are refused by name, and no cut is written for the section:\n  - a machine that is not `wire_edm`, a rotary, `edm.awt: true`;\n  - `WireTaper` not 0, `WireFourAxis`, `WireU` / `WireV`, `WireAngle`;\n  - each `COMP` record (G41 / G42);\n  - skims;\n  - a work offset other than G54;\n  - `SpindleSpeed` above 0, `onToolChange`, `onCycle`, a `Z` change;\n  - `AfterOperation` `home`, `stop` and `optional-stop`;\n  - a second wire section in the same program.\n- Registered in `crates/app/src/posting.rs` (`WIRE_POSTS`) and `crates/app/src/posting_files.rs` (`BUILTINS`, `embedded()`).\n- `crates/app/tests/conformance.rs`: `WIRE_POSTS` and `EXTENSIONS` name the new post.\n- Docs: `assets/posts/AGENTS.md`, the user guide pages `posting.md` and `machines.md`, and `docs/decisions/2700-g-edm-post.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\n`wire-iso.cps` requires `edm.codes.condition` and `edm.codes.comp_off`, and it writes `%` fences. A G-EDM build sets spark power at the controller and has no condition word. A raw Grbl parser rejects `%`. So no shipped post served a G-EDM build.\n\n## Readings\n\n- #2697 has no new answer from the reporter. The unconfirmed items (`F` and Grbl `error:22`, `G40`, `G54`-`G59`, `M0` pauses, a return move) are not written. The decision file gives the reason for each.\n- No `F` word: if G-RBLv3 keeps the Grbl `error:22` check, the controller stops at the first `G1`, before any cut. That is a visible stop, not a wrong cut.\n- One section for each program: without a confirmed `M0`, the program cannot stop to cut the wire and thread it again. A `G0` to a second start point would pull the threaded wire through the work.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins in `crates/app/tests/g_edm_post.rs` (9 tests):\n\n- `g_edm_punch_contour_posts_its_golden_through_the_gate` (golden `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/g-edm/wire_slug_punch.nc`, through `posting::post_script`, machine fixture without `edm.codes`)\n- `g_edm_post_serves_wire_edms_only_and_is_never_the_default`\n- `g_edm_inch_and_arc_words`\n- `g_edm_refuses_taper_four_axis_and_lean_by_name`\n- `g_edm_refuses_radius_compensation_by_name`\n- `g_edm_refuses_skims_by_name`\n- `g_edm_refuses_a_mill_machine_and_a_milling_stream_by_name`\n- `g_edm_refuses_what_the_controller_cannot_be_told`\n- `g_edm_refuses_a_rapid_with_the_wire_threaded_by_name` (review round 1: a rapid between two cuts refuses by name, and no cut follows it)\n\nScript suite `crates/post/tests/script_g_edm.rs`: 11 recorded streams, each a named refusal (`crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/g-edm/`).\n\nRed before the fix: all 8 app pins failed with `built-in post G-EDM Wire EDM is not in the registry`.\n\nMutations (each guard turned off, the pins run, then restored):\n\n- skim guard off: `g_edm_refuses_skims_by_name` red\n- `onRadiusCompensation` guard off: `g_edm_refuses_radius_compensation_by_name` red\n- one-section guard off: `g_edm_refuses_what_the_controller_cannot_be_told` red\n- taper guard off: `g_edm_refuses_taper_four_axis_and_lean_by_name` red\n- rapid-while-threaded guard off (`onRapid`, `if (threaded)`): `g_edm_refuses_a_rapid_with_the_wire_threaded_by_name` red\n- all restored: 9 of 9 green\n\nExpected change: `crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs` counts the shipped text posts. After the merge of main (Mach3 added, Agie native refused), the count goes from 21 to 22. `g-edm.cps` passes every per-post check of that test.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on head `880e5e3d2` (main `f35202134` merged): 797 steps, 0 failed, 1 stalled. The stalled step is `app build (--no-run)`, a cold build after a `cargo clean` with no output for 15 min. Each app suite then built and passed in its own step, `g_edm_post`, `conformance`, `example_catalog` and `mcp_setup_moves` included.\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Heavy lanes\n\nNot run, by rule. AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" (#3556) gives no heavy step to a `P2` or lower PR. This PR is `P6`. The full heavy lanes run at the cut, in the cut gate.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `app suites: example_catalog` passed on head `880e5e3d2`. The new goldens are only under `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/g-edm/` and `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/g-edm/`. No existing golden changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The output was not run on a G-EDM controller or on G-RBLv3.\n- No machine template ships here (#2701).\n- Taper and 4-axis (#2702), and M-codes and skim pauses (#2703), are out of scope.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThese open PRs touch the same files but a different place (other list entries in the same registry tables). Whichever merges second refreshes:\n\n- `crates/app/src/posting_files.rs`, `crates/app/tests/conformance.rs`: #3294, #2646, #2515, and the Agie stack (#2951 .. #2999).\n- `crates/app/src/posting.rs`: #3283, #3160, #3058, and the Agie stack.\n\nChangelog: New \"G-EDM Wire EDM\" post: 2-axis wire contours for G-EDM controllers (G-RBLv3) in Grbl-family words, with no `edm.codes` (spark power is set at the controller); taper, 4-axis, skims and G41 / G42 are refused by name; not verified on a control.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2700\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
